/* book exam traps: Using the piezo signal as absolute pressure. It is relative until pegged: an unpegged trace gives wrong peak pressure and heat release, although the loop area (imep) hardly changes. | Comparing a gross rating with a net rating, or an NEDC emission figure with a WLTC one. Different procedures, different numbers. | Forgetting the factor 2 for a four-stroke: using N/60 instead of N/120 in the imep-to-power step doubles the answer. | Ignoring TDC offset. A one-degree error shifts the peak-pressure angle and changes imep and heat release, because each pressure is paired with the wrong volume. | Quoting COV as a fraction when the question asks for a percentage, or computing COV of peak pressure while calling it COV of imep. */
